# A public loop off the Millrace, with a second way out through the Garden Plots.
Place foundry_court in millrace.
Name: Foundry Court
Description: This was once the yard of a metal factory. Now it is a public square. Under the brick arches are a noticeboard, a drinking fountain, and a table of spare wood. Wide, flat paths lead to every door. The Repair Hall is north. The canal path is east. Northeast takes you back to Millrace. The board lists a walk with six stops and three free things to make.
Outside: yes
Ground: cobble
Smell: Warm brick, sawdust, and cool canal water.
Listen: Water runs beyond the east rail. Through the workshop doorway come brushes on wood and light taps at a bench.
Doings: Open the town guide, follow the Canal trail, or start a project in the Repair Hall.
Northeast: millrace_channel
North: repair_hall
East: canal_towpath
Action: read the foundry board | Read the foundry board | Water once turned the wheels that ran the mills. People now share the old buildings as workshops. A raised line on the board shows the canal path from this square to the garden. You can follow it by touch. This first stop is saved in your notebook. | page | follows the canal path on the foundry noticeboard.

Place repair_hall in millrace.
Name: the Repair Hall
Description: This old machine shop has wide doors and high windows. The work benches come in different heights. Each tool hangs beside a label and an outline of its shape. A tray holds wood for a bird shelter. The pieces are already cut. You can choose a shape, smooth the edges, and put it together. Tools and supplies are free. South leads to Foundry Court. Southeast leads to the canal path.
Outside: no
Ground: wood.interior
Ambience: amb.netloft.room
Smell: Fresh wood shavings, wood oil, and clean cotton aprons.
Listen: Sandpaper brushes wood. Someone taps a small joint into place across the hall.
Doings: Make a bird shelter, inspect the tools, or invite a friend to work alongside you.
South: foundry_court
Southeast: canal_towpath
Action: inspect the tool wall | Inspect the tool wall | You can feel each tool's shape in the raised outline beside it. The label names the tool. The wood is already cut. A clamp holds it still while you work. You can choose a bench at a height that suits you. The Repair Hall is saved in your notebook. | page | explores the labeled tool wall in the Repair Hall.

Place canal_towpath in millrace.
Name: the Canal Towpath
Description: A wide brick path follows the canal. This narrow waterway once carried water to the mills. A rail runs along the path to keep people away from the edge. Marks in the stone wall show old water levels. Benches give you places to rest. West leads to Foundry Court. Northwest leads to the Repair Hall. East leads to the Lock Garden.
Outside: yes
Ground: cobble
Water: canal
Ambience: amb.canal.water
Smell: Wet brick, river moss, and leaves drying on the path.
Listen: A steady stream slides along the wall. Water falls over a low stone ledge farther east.
Doings: Read the water marks, sit with somebody, or follow the rail to the Lock Garden.
West: foundry_court
Northwest: repair_hall
East: lock_garden
Action: read the water marks | Read the water marks | You find three lines cut into the stone wall. The lowest marks low water. The middle shows the level used to run the mill wheels. The highest marks an old flood. You lay paper over the lines and rub a pencil across it to copy their shapes. The copy and a short note go into your notebook. | page | copies the canal water marks into a notebook.

Place lock_garden in sweetwater.
Name: the Lock Garden
Description: A lock is a space between gates that raises or lowers boats with water. This old lock is now a water garden. Water spills over a low stone ledge into tall plants called reeds. A fence keeps the old machines out of reach. A table holds a small model lock you can use. West goes back along the canal path. North leads to the Glass Canopy. East follows a gentle slope to the Canal Overlook.
Outside: yes
Ground: cobble
Water: canal
Ambience: amb.canal.water
Smell: Water mint, wet stone, and the muddy sweetness of reeds.
Listen: Water spills over the ledge nearby. The tall reeds rustle beyond it.
Doings: Try the model lock, examine the reed bed, or take the level path to the Glass Canopy.
West: canal_towpath
North: glass_canopy
East: canal_overlook
Action: examine the reed bed | Examine the reed bed | The reed roots slow the water and catch bits of dirt. The water is clearer after it passes through them. A low planter puts the plants within reach. You feel a rough reed stem, then a smooth mint leaf. Your notebook saves how the garden helps clean the water. | hangout.page | examines the plants beside the old lock.

Place glass_canopy in sweetwater.
Name: the Glass Canopy
Description: An iron frame holds a glass roof over the plant tables. The path between them is wide and flat. Open panels in the roof let fresh air reach the young plants. You can read the labels or feel their raised words. Pots, rich soil, and small herb plants are free to use. South leads to the Lock Garden. West leads to the Garden Plots and Sweetwater Park.
Outside: no
Ground: linoleum
Ambience: amb.reeds.breeze
Smell: Damp soil, mint, and green tomato stems.
Listen: Leaves stir beneath the open vents. A watering can pours into a tray at the far bench.
Doings: Grow an herb cutting, compare the herb labels, or meet a friend at the potting table.
South: lock_garden
West: garden_plots
Action: compare the herbs | Compare the herbs | Mint has a cool smell and a square stem. Rosemary smells a little like pine. Its leaves are narrow and firm. Lemon balm smells like lemon when you gently rub a leaf. You can tell these herbs apart by touch and smell as well as sight. All three go into your notebook. | hangout.page | compares the herb labels and smells beneath the glass roof.

Place canal_overlook in sweetwater.
Name: the Canal Overlook
Description: A gentle slope leads to a wide stone rest area above the lock. A rail runs around its edge. Beside it is a model of the canal, mills, and river, with shapes you can feel. The benches have backs. There is room to turn beside them. West is the only way out. It takes you back to the Lock Garden. The model helps you understand how all the places on your walk fit together.
Outside: yes
Ground: cobble
Water: canal
Ambience: amb.reeds.breeze
Smell: Fresh river air and herbs growing between the stones.
Listen: Water below, leaves behind you, and the distant working hum of Millrace.
Doings: Follow the canal model by touch, read your notebook, or rest on a bench.
West: lock_garden
Action: trace the canal model | Trace the canal model | Your hand follows the water from the river, through the lock, and past the old mills. Each stop on your walk has its own shape on the model. You find the square, workshop, path, garden, and glass roof. Your notebook saves how they connect. The same water once ran machines. Now it feeds plants and gives the town a place to rest. | page | follows the raised canal model by touch.

Link millrace_channel southwest to foundry_court.
Link garden_plots east to glass_canopy.
